{
  "name": "orangutan",
  "_about": "a flanged Bornean orangutan SCULPTED on its rig (2026-11-05, gen: scratchpad sc/prim/gen/orangutan.py, written in its standing pose): a male, the great red ape. Very long arms (a span of some two metres) and short BOWED legs, walking on its FISTS and the curled hand-like feet; a pear of a body -- narrow shoulders over a pot belly; the long shaggy red-orange coat hanging in locks off the backs of its arms, its thighs and its flanks (shag); the FLANGES -- broad cheek pads either side of a small flat grey face -- a pendulous throat sac under a russet beard, small close-set forward-facing eyes, small ears (2026-11-08: the mesh budget re-spread -- the focus had given the head and the four hands some 13800 of 14100 faces and the whole trunk 68, a low-poly body cut differently left and right; now 12000/3600 with focus head 3, hands 2.5, feet 2, the trunk ~2200 -- and, a mirror-symmetric field, meshed as its half and reflected: exactly symmetric; the ears smaller and flatter to the head) (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): small flat shells close to the head (sharp.js `fin`), rooted along their front edge, the hollow out and forward, its fold (the helix) a band of the outer colour; the roots faired.",
